<title>ITALY: Eni to underwrite Albacom capital increase.</title>
<headline>Eni to underwrite Albacom capital increase.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian energy group Eni said on Thursday it would underwrite a 173 billion lire capital increase at Anglo-Italian mobile phone operator Albacom.</p>
<p>Eni announced the deal at a news conference at which it also said it was taking a 35 percent stake in Albacom and becoming its biggest shareholder. Albacom's other shareholders are British Telecommunications Plc, Italy's Banca Nazionale del Lavoro and communications group Mediaset.  </p>
<p>Alfred Mockett, BT managing director for global communications, told reporters at the news conference that the current value of Albacom was 500 billion lire.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
</text>
